Short description
-----------------

df1:

 Deformation fields for a steady Stokes flow.
 Problem 1: Flow based on the stokes2 problem
   Stokes problem on a unit square. Periodical boundary conditions.
   Poiseuille flow.
   Collocation of nodes.
 Problem 2: Deformation fields computed as a function of time (problem 2),
   assuming the flow starts instantaneously at t=0 and was at rest for t<0.
 Decoupled fields, explicit DG with P1 interpolation for tau-convection
   (similar to the 2001 paper).
 Extrapolated BDF2 time discretization.

df2:

 Deformation fields for a steady Stokes flow.
 Problem 1: Flow based on the stokes2 problem
   Stokes problem on a unit square. Periodical boundary conditions.
   Poiseuille flow.
   Collocation of nodes.
 Problem 2: Deformation fields computed as a function of time (problem 2),
   assuming the flow starts instantaneously at t=0 and was at rest for t<0.
 Decoupled fields, explicit DG with P2 interpolation for tau-convection
   (similar to the 2001 paper).
 Extrapolated BDF3 time discretization.

 Similar to df1, but with the changes
 explicit DG with P2 interpolation
 Extrapolated BDF3 time discretization.

df3: 

 Deformation fields for a steady Stokes flow.
 Problem 1: Flow based on the stokes2 problem
   Stokes problem on a unit square. Periodical boundary conditions.
   Poiseuille flow.
   Collocation of nodes.
 Problem 2: Deformation fields computed as a function of time (problem 2),
   assuming the flow starts instantaneously at t=0 and was at rest for t<0.
 Implicit DG with P1 or P2 interpolation for tau-convection.
 Extrapolated BDF2 time discretization.

df4: 

 Deformation fields for a steady Stokes flow.
 Problem 1: Stokes flow around a confined cylinder.
   Periodical boundary conditions.
 Problem 2: Deformation fields computed as a function of time, assuming the
   flow starts instantaneously at t=0 and was at rest for t<0.
 Implicit DG with P1 or P2 interpolation for tau-convection.
 Extrapolated BDF2 time discretization.
 Some CPU savings for equidistant grids in tau, since matrix is the same for
 all intervals.

df5:

 Deformation fields for a steady Stokes flow.
 Problem 1: Flow based on the stokes2 problem
   Stokes problem on a unit square. Periodical boundary conditions.
   Poiseuille flow.
   Collocation of nodes.
 Problem 2: Deformation fields computed as a function of time (problem 2),
   assuming the flow starts instantaneously at t=0 and was at rest for t<0.
 Decoupled fields, explicit DG with P1 interpolation for tau-convection
   (similar to the 2001 paper).
 Extrapolated BDF2 time discretization.

 Problem based on df1 with the extension:
 Compute stress tensor for an integral model (postprocessing only).

df6:

 Deformation fields for a steady Stokes flow.
 Problem 1: Flow based on the stokes2 problem
   Stokes problem on a unit square. Periodical boundary conditions.
   Poiseuille flow.
   Collocation of nodes.
 Problem 2: Deformation fields computed as a function of time (problem 2),
   assuming the flow starts instantaneously at t=0 and was at rest for t<0.
 Implicit DG with P1 or P2 interpolation for tau-convection.
 Extrapolated BDF2 time discretization.

 Problem based on df3 with the extension:
 Compute stress tensor for an integral model (postprocessing only).

df7:

 Deformation fields for a steady Stokes flow.
 Problem 1: Stokes flow around a confined cylinder.
   Periodical boundary conditions.
 Problem 2: Deformation fields computed as a function of time, assuming the
   flow starts instantaneously at t=0 and was at rest for t<0.
 Implicit DG with P1 or P2 interpolation for tau-convection.
 Extrapolated BDF2 time discretization.
 Some CPU savings for equidistant grids in tau, since matrix is the same for
 all intervals.

 Problem based on df4 with the extension:
 Compute stress tensor for an integral model (postprocessing only).

df8:

 Deformation fields for a steady Stokes flow.
 Problem 1: Flow based on the stokes2 problem
   Stokes problem on a unit square. Periodical boundary conditions.
   Poiseuille flow.
   Collocation of nodes.
 Problem 2: Deformation fields computed as a function of time (problem 2),
   assuming the flow starts instantaneously at t=0 and was at rest for t<0.
 Implicit DG with P1 or P2 interpolation for tau-convection.
 Extrapolated BDF2 time discretization.

 Problem based on df6 with the extension:
 Compute stress tensor for an integral model by L2-projection on the finite
 element approximation space of the deformation gradient tensor
 (postprocessing only).

df9:

 Deformation fields for a steady Stokes flow.
 Problem 1: Stokes flow around a confined cylinder.
   Periodical boundary conditions.
 Problem 2: Deformation fields computed as a function of time, assuming the
   flow starts instantaneously at t=0 and was at rest for t<0.
 Implicit DG with P1 or P2 interpolation for tau-convection.
 Extrapolated BDF2 time discretization.
 Some CPU savings for equidistant grids in tau, since matrix is the same for
 all intervals.

 Problem based on df7 with the extension:
 Compute stress tensor for an integral model by L2-projection on the finite
 element approximation space of the deformation gradient tensor
 (postprocessing only).

df10:

 Startup of Poiseuille flow for an integral model.
 Problem 1: 
   Poiseuille flow on a unit square. Periodical boundary conditions.
   Collocation of nodes.
   Stress-implicit formulation of the momentum balance.
 Problem 2: Deformation fields computed as a function of time, assuming the
   flow starts instantaneously at t=0 and was at rest for t<0.
 Problem 3: Stress tensor projection on the interpolation space for F.
 Implicit DG with P1 or P2 interpolation for tau-convection.
 Extrapolated BDF2 time discretization.

df11:

 Startup of flow around a cylinder for an integral model.
 Problem 1: Flow around a confined cylinder.
   Periodical boundary conditions.
   Stress-implicit formulation of the momentum balance.
 Problem 2: Deformation fields computed as a function of time, assuming the
   flow starts instantaneously at t=0 and was at rest for t<0.
 Problem 3: Stress tensor projection on the interpolation space for F.
 Implicit DG with P1 or P2 interpolation for tau-convection.
 Extrapolated BDF2 time discretization.
 Some CPU savings for equidistant grids in tau, since matrix is the same for
 all intervals.
